From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Feb 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: initialize SQ_GPR_MANAGEMENT for A22X

The SQ_GPR_MANAGEMENT register (0x0D00) controls how shader GPRs
(General Purpose Registers) are allocated between vertex and pixel
shaders on A2XX GPUs.

KGSL (the proprietary Qualcomm GPU driver) initializes this register
to 0x00040400, which allocates 64 GPRs each for vertex and pixel
shaders. Freedreno does not initialize this register, leaving it with
undefined values after GPU power-on.

Register layout:
  REG_DYNAMIC (bit 0): dynamic vs static allocation
  REG_SIZE_PIX (bits 4-11): GPRs available for pixel shader
  REG_SIZE_VTX (bits 12-19): GPRs available for vertex shader

When uninitialized, random values can cause:
- GPR starvation in vertex or pixel shader stages
- Insufficient registers for varying interpolation
- Intermittent faceted shading when smooth shading is expected

This explains why the same shader code sometimes produces smooth
output and sometimes produces faceted output - it depends on what
random value the GPU power-on state left in this register.

Symptoms fixed:
- Intermittent faceted vs smooth surfaces in glmark2 build benchmark
- Random normal interpolation failures in GLES2 applications

Upstream-Status: Pending
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c
index 1ceb900..a2b3c01 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c
@@ -555,6 +555,20 @@ fd2_emit_restore(struct fd_context *ctx, struct fd_ringbuffer *ring)
    OUT_RING(ring, 0x5f601000);
    OUT_RING(ring, 0x00000001);

+   /* A22X: Initialize SQ_GPR_MANAGEMENT to allocate 64 GPRs each for vertex
+    * and pixel shaders. KGSL initializes this to 0x00040400. Without proper
+    * initialization, a random value from GPU power-on could starve one
+    * shader type of GPRs, causing intermittent varying interpolation issues
+    * (e.g., faceted shading when smooth shading is expected).
+    *
+    * Register layout (0x0d00):
+    *   REG_DYNAMIC (bit 0): 0 = static allocation
+    *   REG_SIZE_PIX (bits 4-11): 0x40 = 64 GPRs for pixel shader
+    *   REG_SIZE_VTX (bits 12-19): 0x40 = 64 GPRs for vertex shader
+    */
+   OUT_PKT0(ring, REG_A2XX_SQ_GPR_MANAGEMENT, 1);
+   OUT_RING(ring, 0x00040400);
+
    OUT_PKT0(ring, REG_A2XX_SQ_INST_STORE_MANAGMENT, 1);
    OUT_RING(ring, 0x00000180);

